Now I can see clearly! This is a custom GenAI Grounding tool that uses Google Search grounding. Let me explain and guide you on how to use it.

What This Tool Does
From the description:
	∙	Submits a user prompt to a GenAI inference engine
	∙	Grounded using enterprise web search powered by Google Search
	∙	Requires api_key and app_code for authentication
	∙	Returns model-generated result based on grounded information
So basically it’s LLM + Google Search combined in one API call!

Tool Details

Name: prompt_admin_post
Method: POST
Path: /genai-infer/api/prompt_admin
Auth: api_key + app_code (in headers)


Step 1: Test It in Postman First

curl -X POST "https://your-base-url/genai-infer/api/prompt_admin" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "api_key: your_api_key" \
  -H "app_code: your_app_code" \
  -d '{
    "prompt": "Give me a public profile of Elon Musk including his background, career and recent news"
  }'


Test this first and confirm you get a response — then we use it in Dify.

Step 2: Use It in Dify Workflow
Once confirmed working, here’s the simple flow:

[START] person_name
    ↓
[LLM Node] - Generate search prompt
    ↓
[HTTP Request Node] - Call grounding tool
    ↓
[LLM Node] - Format final report
    ↓
[END]


START Node

Variable: person_name (string)


LLM Node - Build Prompt

System: You are a prompt generator.

User: Create a detailed search prompt to find public 
profile information about: {{#start.person_name#}}

Include: background, career, recent news, affiliations


HTTP Request Node

Method: POST
URL: https://your-base-url/genai-infer/api/prompt_admin
Headers:
  Content-Type: application/json
  api_key: your_api_key
  app_code: your_app_code
Body (JSON):
{
  "prompt": "{{#llm.text#}}"
}


Final LLM Node - Format Report

System: You are a professional profiling analyst.

User: Format this grounded search result into a 
clean public profile report:

{{#http.body#}}

Format:
## Public Profile: [Name]
**Summary:**
**Career:**
**Recent News:**
**Key Facts:**


